<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Income tax: deductions, reliefs and PAYE (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>In a simplified tax system, all taxable income is taxed at a single rate of \( {@r0@}\% \). {@nm@} has a monthly taxable income of Ksh \( {@TI@} \), and is entitled to a personal relief of Ksh 2,400 and an insurance relief of Ksh \( {@ir@} \) each month.</p>
<p>(a) Calculate the gross tax.</p>
<div>Gross tax \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) Calculate the tax actually paid (PAYE).</p>
<div>PAYE \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a)</strong> Gross tax \( = {@TI@} \times \frac{ {@r0@} }{100} = {@gt@} \).</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> Reliefs are subtracted from the <em>tax</em>, after it has been calculated:</p>
\[ \text{PAYE} = {@gt@} - 2{,}400 - {@ir@} = {@paye@}. \]
<p>Deductions (like NSSF) reduce the <em>income</em> before tax is worked out; reliefs reduce the <em>tax</em> itself. Subtracting the reliefs from the income instead would give \( {@r2(w_asded)@} \), which is wrong.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025010100</text>
